From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin <robinei@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 18:48:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915/dsi: Set the MIPI C HS TX delay on CHV

EXPERIMENT, not for upstream.

MIPIA_PORT_CTRL holds HS TX clock delay fields for MIPI C (bits 15,
14:11 and 7:5, VLV PRM vol 10) that i915 and the GOP leave at the
default (one buffer delay); the PRM says they must be set "to a value
determined by clock timing team". Intel's Android kernel had a CHV
A0-A3 workaround for "bad clock timing on the MIPI data lanes" that
set the corresponding fields of the port's own register (0xe82d0000:
MIPI4DPHY delay 13, FLISDSI delay 11). A GPD Pocket with the same
intermittent DSI misalignment as our GPD Win 1 was fine after a
mainboard swap, which points at per-unit timing margin. Try the same
delays for MIPI C.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c
index 8f5911c..c534146 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c
@@ -630,6 +630,19 @@ static void intel_dsi_port_enable(struct intel_encoder *encoder,
 		}
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * EXPERIMENT: HS TX delay for MIPI C. Its delay fields live in port
+	 * A's port control register (VLV PRM vol 10, MIPIA_PORT_CTRL bits 15,
+	 * 14:11, 7:5; default 0 = 1 buffer delay, "value determined by clock
+	 * timing team"). Use the values Intel's CHV A0-A3 workaround used for
+	 * the port's own fields (0xe82d0000: MIPI4DPHY 13, FLISDSI 11).
+	 */
+	if (display->platform.cherryview &&
+	    intel_dsi->ports == BIT(PORT_C))
+		intel_de_rmw(display, port_ctrl_reg(display, PORT_A),
+			     BIT(15) | GENMASK(14, 11) | GENMASK(7, 5),
+			     (13 << 11) | BIT(15) | (3 << 5));
+
 	for_each_dsi_port(port, intel_dsi->ports) {
 		intel_reg_t port_ctrl = port_ctrl_reg(display, port);
 		u32 temp;
